  "strategy": "Approach and rationale\nWe address the Erd\u0151s minimum overlap problem by evolving a step function representation through a generational algorithm with adaptive crossover and mutation operators. Unlike traditional optimization methods that focus on local improvements, this approach explores a diverse set of parent functions through coarse-grained population dynamics. The key rationale is that the optimal solution likely combines structural features from different parent configurations, which single-point optimization tends to miss. We introduce a novel evaluation metric based on linear cross-correlation properties, ensure valid function representations through repair mechanisms, and apply genetic operations that respect the integral constraint. This method systematically explores the entire search space by balancing exploration and exploitation phases, and iteratively refines solutions through directed mutation mechanisms.\n\nMathematical specification\nThe function space is represented as periodic step functions with discontinuities handled through weighted interpolation. Specifically, a function is defined by:\n\u2022 A base resolution of 160 points covering [0,2]\n\u2022 Function values h(x) \u2208 [0,1] with \u222b\u2080\u00b2 h(x)dx = 1\n\u2022 Periodicity: h(x+2) = h(x)\n\nThe overlap integral C\u2085 is defined as:\nC\u2085 = sup\u2096 \u222b\u2080\u00b2\u207b\u1d4f h(x)(1-h(x+k))dx\nDiscrete evaluation: max_k \u2211\u1d62 h[i]|\u2081-h[i+k]| * dx (circular mode)\n\nImplementation procedure\n1. Parent population initialization:\n   - Primary parents: Linear transformation of given `initial_h_values`\n   - Secondary parents: Regular grids (binary, rectangular, etc.)\n   - Tertiary parents: Brownian bridges from random boundary crossings\n\n2. Fitness evaluation:\n   a. Compute cross-correlation: corr[k] = \u2211\u1d62 h[i]|\u2081-h[i+k]| * dx\n   b. C\u2085 = max{corr[k]} (without dx scaling for direct comparison)\n   c. Additional scaling factor: \u03b2(dx\u00b2 / \u2211\u1d62 (h[i] - mean)\u00b2)\n\n3. Selection mechanism:\n   - Generational selection based on C\u2085 scores\n   - Survival of top 10% (depends on population size)\n   - Tournament selection with elitism\n\n4. Crossover operations (multi-point with adaptive segment widths):\n   - Segment width proportional to fitness rank\n   - Weighted combination preserving local harmonic properties\n\n5. Mutation operators:\n   a. Directional mutation: Local function perturbations following genetic programming principles\n   b. Constraint-aware mutation: Gradient direction optimization with integral preservation\n   c. Diversity maintenance: Random harmonic displacement applied to isolated parents\n\n6. Repair code fragment ensuring 0\u2264h[i]\u22641 and integral=1:\n```python\ndef repair_h(h_vec, target_integral):\n    current_sum = np.sum(h_vec)\n    adjusted_h = h_vec + (target_integral - current_sum) / len(h_vec)\n    adjusted_h = np.clip(adjusted_h, 0.0, 1.0)\n    # Linear adjustment ensures integral preservation\n    return adjusted_h + (target_integral - np.sum(adjusted_h)/len(adjusted_h)) * (1/len(h_vec)) * np.random.randn(len(adjusted_h))\n```\n\nSearch choices and variations\n- Population sizing: 30-40 individuals (computational trade-off)\n- Mutation rates: Amplitude 0.1-0.3 (depends on generation)\n- Selection pressure: 3:1 replacement ratio\n- Repertoire of mutation operators: 6 distinct operators employed systematically\n\nComputational budget and robustness\n- Each generation: 15 crossover attempts, 35 mutation events\n- Generational speed: \u223c120 seconds (conservative estimate)\n- Total timeline: 16 generations within 1920-second budget\n- Early termination: 20% improvement threshold over last 3 generations\n- Time safeguards: Dynamic operation scaling based on elapsed time\n\nValidation and return contract\n1. Verify \u2211h[i] * dx = 1 to \u00b11e-6 (relative tolerance)\n2. Ensure all h[i] \u2208 [0,1] after repair\n3. Run final parent loop with 5 local optimizations\n4. Compute C\u2085 using circular convolution of original samples\n5. Return values meet format: (h_values, c5_bound, n_points=160)\n6. Diversity maintenance: 3 separate runs with distinct mutation spectra",
